pt-PT.txt.gz is a pronouncing dictionary of Portuguese (Portugal),
generated by the program in ptpt/, beside this file, from three sources:

- Its words come from the European Portuguese Hunspell dictionary, as
  LibreOffice ships it (https://github.com/LibreOffice/dictionaries, pt_PT),
  at commit fe49c662796b47cb19732d18114610a58848f5cb. Modified: each word is
  kept with the forms its suffixes make, leaving out rare verb tenses, names
  and abbreviations.
- Their pronunciations are made by eSpeak NG, version 1.51.1
  (https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng), with its European Portuguese
  voice. Modified: written in one phone set, with a stress digit on each
  vowel, and some sounds it gets wrong corrected.
- Whether a word's stressed vowel is open or closed is corrected from
  Wiktionary's pronunciations of it (https://en.wiktionary.org/), by
  Wiktionary's contributors, as WikiPron gathers them
  (https://github.com/CUNY-CL/wikipron, data/scrape/tsv/por_latn_po_broad.tsv,
  at commit d282e848a211ea31cfd730f0ced8bc8cdab9e83d):

    Jackson L. Lee, Lucas F.E. Ashby, M. Elizabeth Garza, Yeonju Lee-Sikka,
    Sean Miller, Alan Wong, Arya D. McCarthy, and Kyle Gorman (2020).
    Massively multilingual pronunciation mining with WikiPron. In
    Proceedings of the 12th Language Resources and Evaluation Conference,
    pages 4223-4228. https://aclanthology.org/2020.lrec-1.521/

  Then ptpt/overrides.txt, checked by hand, corrects the rest.

Each source's licence lets pt-PT.txt.gz ship in Bandmate, under the GNU
Affero General Public License, version 3:

- The Hunspell dictionary is offered under the GPL, LGPL or MPL. Bandmate
  uses it under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1
  (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html), section 3 of
  which lets it be used under the GNU General Public License instead.
- eSpeak NG is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
  later (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html), section 13 of which
  lets it be combined with a work under the GNU Affero General Public
  License, version 3.
- Wiktionary's text is licensed under the Creative Commons
  Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), as its copyright page
  says (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiktionary:Copyrights). Creative
  Commons lists version 3 of the GNU General Public License as compatible
  with it (https://creativecommons.org/compatiblelicenses/).

So pt-PT.txt.gz is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3.
It comes with no warranties. The sources' notices follow.

